Yes. The game checks the possibility of bones files for the level only
when the game ends, not when you arrive to a new level. When a level is
created, the game always checks whether or not there is a bones file, even
on no-bones levels.
I just verified this by starting a wizard-mode game, throwing my weapons
up until I got the die [y/n] prompt and answered yes to that and the other
prompt for leaving bones.
Then I kept on starting a normal game and quitting until I got the bones
file loaded. It took eight starts, but finally the bones got loaded.
(And next I will remove those eight test entries from my logfile..)

> otherwise that would make no sense

Why not? Wizard-mode bones are not actually supposed to be left to be
consumed in a real game, so it would make perfect sense to me to load them
only in other wizard mode games.
(But there is no flag in the bones file that would clearly mark it as a
wizard mode file, so there is no way for the game to tell them apart.)

